@title Drift Harbor client patch rollback
@subtitle Runbook for rolling back a bad game client patch
@author Quillfeather Interactive, Live Ops
@date 2026-10-13

kpi Crash rate trigger | > 2% | for 15 min | bad
kpi Login failure trigger | > 5% | for 10 min | bad
kpi Last good build | 4.12.3 | rollback target | neutral
kpi Approval | Live Ops lead | #liveops-war-room | neutral

!!! Never roll back after a database schema migration: it corrupts player inventories. Go forward with a hotfix instead.

# When to roll back
After a patch release, roll back when either is true:
- Crash rate above 2% of sessions for 15 minutes.
- Login failures above 5% for 10 minutes.

! The Live Ops lead must approve the rollback in the `#liveops-war-room` channel.

# Do not roll back if
The patch contained a database schema migration, such as migration 0087 in patch 4.13. Older clients cannot read the new schema, so go forward with a hotfix instead.

# Rollback steps
1. Stop the bleeding
-- 1. Pause the deploy pipeline.
-- 2. Set matchmaking to maintenance mode with the in-game message "Back soon".
2. Point players to the last good build
-- 1. In the release console, set the live manifest to build 4.12.3.
-- 2. Invalidate the CDN cache (takes about 10 minutes).
3. Verify
-- 1. Install the build on 3 test accounts, one each on PC, console and mobile.
-- 2. Confirm login and a full match.
4. Reopen in stages
-- 1. Let in 10% of players.
-- 2. 25% after 5 minutes.
-- 3. 50% after 5 more minutes.
-- 4. 100% after another 5 minutes, if the crash rate stays under 1%.
5. Communicate
-- 1. Post a status update within 30 minutes of the decision.
-- 2. Schedule compensation of 500 gems for every active account.

